        {'id': 'Q22', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Generative AI: Temperature Tuning', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You want to configure an LLM application to write cold marketing emails. You want the output language to be highly imaginative, varied, and creative, intentionally avoiding repetitive structural paths across subsequent generations.', 'question': 'Which parameter setting is MOST suitable?', 'options': ['Set Temperature to 0.0', 'Set Temperature to 0.9', 'Disable System Prompts', 'Reduce maximum token count to 5'], 'correct_answer': 'Set Temperature to 0.9', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Higher temperature values (closer to 1.0) increase structural randomness, encouraging creative and highly varied vocabulary output.', 'incorrect': 'Temperature 0.0 forces determinism. Disabling prompts degrades behavior. Restricting tokens to 5 cuts off outputs.', 'concept': 'LLM parameters: Temperature.'}, 'avg_time': 40, 'confused_services': ['temperature', 'tokens']},
        {'id': 'Q23', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Generative AI: RAG Pipeline Sequencing', 'type': 'dropdown-hotspot', 'scenario': 'Arrange the RAG conceptual processing steps in the correct operational chronological sequence from raw document ingestion to answering a user query.', 'question': 'Select the correct sequence order number (1 to 4) for each step.', 'parts': [{'text': 'The user submits an interactive conversational query regarding corporate parental leave policies: Step ', 'options': ['1', '2', '3', '4'], 'answer': '2'}, {'text': ". The Azure AI Search index retrieves highly relevant document chunks based on vector embeddings matching the user's intent: Step ", 'options': ['1', '2', '3', '4'], 'answer': '3'}, {'text': '. Raw HR policy documents are chunked, transformed into vector embeddings, and ingested into an Azure AI Search vector store: Step ', 'options': ['1', '2', '3', '4'], 'answer': '1'}, {'text': '. The Azure OpenAI LLM receives the prompt injected with matching document contexts and generates a grounded response: Step ', 'options': ['1', '2', '3', '4'], 'answer': '4'}], 'correct_answer': ['2', '3', '1', '4'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'First, raw assets must be chunked and indexed into vector space (1). Later, a user submits a query (2). The system searches the vector index to retrieve matching text segments (3). Finally, the LLM generates a grounded answer based on that retrieved context (4).', 'incorrect': 'Review RAG architecture ingestion-to-query sequences.', 'concept': 'RAG ingestion and query execution workflow.'}, 'avg_time': 75, 'confused_services': ['rag-sequence']},
        {'id': 'Q24', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Generative AI: LLM Base Capabilities', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'Which of the following describes a core foundational capability of an LLM base model without retrieval enhancements or fine-tuning?', 'question': 'Select the correct capability description.', 'options': ['Running live hardware telemetry diagnostics on server clusters.', 'Predicting the token next in sequence based on probabilistic distributions learned during pre-training.', 'Storing permanent user credit card transactions securely within its weights.', 'Automatically updating its internal weights with real-time news articles via internet scraping.'], 'correct_answer': 'Predicting the token next in sequence based on probabilistic distributions learned during pre-training.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'At their fundamental technical level, autoregressive Large Language Models are sophisticated token prediction mechanisms that estimate the next most likely word fragment using probability tables.', 'incorrect': 'LLMs do not run server telemetry, encrypt credit cards inside weights, or auto-scrape real-time news to modify parameters dynamically.', 'concept': 'Autoregressive LLM mechanics.'}, 'avg_time': 40, 'confused_services': ['llms', 'model-training']},
        {'id': 'Q25', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure AI Language: Custom Classification', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A retail firm wants to build an automated application that routes incoming social media posts to customer success queues. If a post contains explicit statements regarding broken items, it must route to Warranty; if it contains questions about pricing, it must route to Sales.', 'question': 'Which capability of Azure AI Language is MOST appropriate?', 'options': ['Custom Text Classification', 'Named Entity Recognition (NER)', 'Language Detection', 'Conversational Language Understanding (CLU) only for slot filling'], 'correct_answer': 'Custom Text Classification', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Custom Text Classification within Azure AI Language allows users to train a model to assign custom categorical tags (e.g., Warranty, Sales) to full blocks of text based on historical examples.', 'incorrect': 'NER extracts standard entities. Language detection finds the spoken tongue. CLU is designed for dialogue intent extraction, not general full-document routing classifications.', 'concept': 'Azure AI Language: Custom Text Classification.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['classification', 'clu']},
        {'id': 'Q26', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Responsible AI: Transparency', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A company deploys an AI credit assessment scoring tool. They provide a published comprehensive framework detailing exactly which architectural models were selected, what types of training metadata were collected, and how individual scoring results are calculated.', 'question': 'This directly maps to which Responsible AI principle?', 'options': ['Fairness', 'Privacy and Security', 'Transparency', 'Inclusiveness'], 'correct_answer': 'Transparency', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Providing open, visible information regarding model architecture selection, collected training assets, and operational logic directly fulfills the Transparency principle.', 'incorrect': 'Fairness avoids bias. Privacy protects records. Inclusiveness handles accessibility.', 'concept': 'Responsible AI: Transparency principle.'}, 'avg_time': 40, 'confused_services': ['transparency', 'accountability']},
        {'id': 'Q27', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure AI Vision: Workloads', 'type': 'true-false-matrix', 'scenario': 'For each of the following statements regarding Azure AI Vision capabilities, select Yes if the statement is true, otherwise select No.', 'statements': [{'text': 'Object detection identifies individual objects within an image, classifies them, and provides spatial bounding box coordinates.', 'answer': 'Yes'}, {'text': 'Image classification evaluates an entire image and applies a categorical label, but does not identify spatial layout boundaries of distinct objects.', 'answer': 'Yes'}, {'text': 'The Face API can evaluate facial landmarks and geometry, but cannot perform identity verification against an approved image gallery due to fundamental design limitations.', 'answer': 'No'}], 'correct_answer': ['Yes', 'Yes', 'No'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'Object detection provides bounding boxes. Classification tags whole images without spatial limits. The Face API contains advanced features designed explicitly to match and verify identities against galleries (rendering Row 3 false).', 'incorrect': 'Review the differences between image classification and object detection.', 'concept': 'Azure AI Vision capabilities differentiation.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['classification', 'object-detection', 'face']},
        {'id': 'Q28', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Prompt Engineering: Few-shot', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You provide an LLM with five explicit examples of customer complaints alongside their corresponding target JSON classification formats within the text prompt itself before adding the actual user complaint text.', 'question': 'What prompt engineering technique does this represent?', 'options': ['Zero-shot learning', 'Few-shot learning', 'Fine-tuning', 'Prompt injection'], 'correct_answer': 'Few-shot learning', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Supplying a small set of concrete examples directly inside the text prompt context window to demonstrate desired output patterns is called few-shot learning.', 'incorrect': 'Zero-shot includes no examples. Fine-tuning alters model weights via backpropagation. Prompt injection is an exploit.', 'concept': 'Few-shot learning in prompt designs.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['few-shot', 'zero-shot']},
        {'id': 'Q29', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Azure AI Foundry: Features', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A software development firm needs to build a chat interface that answers developer questions about open-source code libraries. They want to leverage pre-built foundational frontier models like GPT-4o with integrated corporate enterprise data compliance guarantees.', 'question': 'Which Azure platform environment is the central unified location to deploy these generative models?', 'options': ['Azure AI Foundry', 'Azure Data Factory', 'Azure Cosmos DB', 'Azure DevOps Services'], 'correct_answer': 'Azure AI Foundry', 'explanations': {'correct': "Azure AI Foundry is Microsoft's unified development platform to explore, build, test, and deploy enterprise generative AI solutions and frontier models.", 'incorrect': 'Data Factory manages pipelines. Cosmos DB is a database. DevOps handles CI/CD.', 'concept': 'Azure AI Foundry centralized architecture.'}, 'avg_time': 30, 'confused_services': ['studio', 'azure-portal']},
        {'id': 'Q30', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Responsible AI: Privacy & Security', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'An AI system used for automated dental analysis unintentionally exposes confidential medical radiographs through unencrypted local cached storage endpoints.', 'question': 'This failure violates which Microsoft Responsible AI principle?', 'options': ['Accountability', 'Privacy and Security', 'Fairness', 'Inclusiveness'], 'correct_answer': 'Privacy and Security', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Leaving highly sensitive personal medical records unencrypted in accessible storage endpoints represents a critical breakdown of the Privacy and Security standard.', 'incorrect': 'Accountability handles oversight. Fairness targets bias. Inclusiveness handles accessibility.', 'concept': 'Responsible AI: Privacy and Security principle.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['privacy-security', 'accountability']},
        {'id': 'Q31', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure AI Language: Native Features', 'type': 'multi-choice', 'scenario': 'Which two workloads represent specific native features of Azure AI Language?', 'question': 'Select TWO options.', 'options': ['Summarization of unstructured meeting transcripts.', 'Transcribing human audio streams into text files.', 'Named Entity Recognition (NER) to extract locations, names, and organizations.', 'Generating synthetic human vocal streams from plain text.'], 'correct_answer': ['Summarization of unstructured meeting transcripts.', 'Named Entity Recognition (NER) to extract locations, names, and organizations.'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'Document/transcript summarization and Named Entity Recognition (NER) are native textual services housed inside Azure AI Language.', 'incorrect': 'Audio transcription and vocal stream generation belong to Azure AI Speech services.', 'concept': 'Azure AI Language features.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['language', 'speech']},
        {'id': 'Q32', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Generative AI: System Prompts', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': "What is the primary role of a 'System Prompt' in a generative AI conversational environment?", 'question': 'Select the primary role description.', 'options': ['To evaluate the monetary execution cost of the chat transaction.', 'To set the baseline context, persona, behavior boundaries, and core guidelines for the LLM.', 'To compress text documents before storage ingestion.', 'To establish firewall protection parameters for the host network.'], 'correct_answer': 'To set the baseline context, persona, behavior boundaries, and core guidelines for the LLM.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'System prompts are instructions that hardcode institutional behavioral guardrails, conversational alignment profiles, and operational tasks for an LLM before user interaction starts.', 'incorrect': 'System prompts do not compute token costs, compress database records, or set firewall configurations.', 'concept': 'Role of System Prompts.'}, 'avg_time': 30, 'confused_services': ['system-prompt', 'user-prompt']},
        {'id': 'Q33', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Conversational AI: Agents vs Chatbots', 'type': 'true-false-matrix', 'scenario': 'For each of the following statements regarding AI Agents and Conversational AI, select Yes if the statement is true, otherwise select No.', 'statements': [{'text': 'An AI Agent can orchestrate actions, leverage external tools, and query knowledge retrieval bases dynamically based on user goals.', 'answer': 'Yes'}, {'text': 'Standard chatbots always require explicit human hardcoded branching trees and cannot use natural language understanding algorithms.', 'answer': 'No'}, {'text': 'Azure AI Foundry provides orchestration capabilities to build custom multi-agent workflows.', 'answer': 'Yes'}], 'correct_answer': ['Yes', 'No', 'Yes'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'Agents evaluate intent and call tools. Chatbots regularly utilize NLP models rather than strictly hardcoded branching code trees. Azure AI Foundry supports multi-agent orchestrations.', 'incorrect': 'Review difference between chatbots and agents.', 'concept': 'AI Agents and Conversational AI logic.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['chatbot', 'agent']},
        {'id': 'Q34', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure AI Vision: Spatial Analysis', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'An automotive security manufacturer needs a system to analyze video footage from a standard parking garage camera to detect when cars enter illegal zones and alert security teams.', 'question': 'Which Azure service should be deployed for this real-time spatial video and spatial tracking workload?', 'options': ['Azure AI Language', 'Azure AI Document Intelligence', 'Azure AI Vision (Spatial Analysis)', 'Azure OpenAI Whisper'], 'correct_answer': 'Azure AI Vision (Spatial Analysis)', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Azure AI Vision Spatial Analysis is engineered to evaluate live real-time video feeds to track spatial positions, presence, and movement of items or persons within geometric zones.', 'incorrect': 'Language parses text. Document Intelligence reads documents. Whisper transcribes speech.', 'concept': 'Azure AI Vision Spatial Analysis workloads.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['spatial-analysis', 'face']},
        {'id': 'Q35', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Generative AI: Foundation Models', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'Which technical concept describes a transformer-based machine learning architecture trained on massive web-scale corpora that serves as the upstream core starting point for down-stream generative tasks?', 'question': 'Select the correct concept term.', 'options': ['Support Vector Machine', 'Linear Regression Node', 'Foundation Model', 'Decision Tree Forest'], 'correct_answer': 'Foundation Model', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Foundation models are large scale upstream transformer systems trained on massive general datasets that can be easily adapted to distinct downstream generative capabilities.', 'incorrect': 'SVM, linear regression, and decision tree forests are traditional machine learning algorithms, not pre-trained transformer foundation models.', 'concept': 'Foundation model definitions.'}, 'avg_time': 30, 'confused_services': ['foundation-models', 'model-training']},
        {'id': 'Q36', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Generative AI: Vector Embeddings', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You are configuring an instance of Azure AI Search as part of a generative AI pipeline. You need to convert unstructured documents into high-dimensional numerical vectors that capture semantic meaning.', 'question': 'What capability or model type do you need to deploy within Azure OpenAI to generate these coordinates?', 'options': ['DALL-E 3', 'GPT-4o-mini', 'Text Embedding Model (e.g., text-embedding-3-small)', 'Whisper Speech Model'], 'correct_answer': 'Text Embedding Model (e.g., text-embedding-3-small)', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Text embedding models are explicitly designed to translate words and phrases into mathematical vectors that represent their core semantic meaning within high-dimensional space.', 'incorrect': 'DALL-E generates images. GPT-4o-mini is for chat text generation. Whisper transcribes audio.', 'concept': 'Embeddings model capabilities.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['embeddings', 'chat-completion']},
        {'id': 'Q37', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Prompt Engineering: Terms', 'type': 'drag-drop', 'scenario': 'Match each specific prompt engineering term to its corresponding definition or core operational trait.', 'question': 'Match each term to the correct definition.', 'draggableItems': ['Zero-shot', 'Chain-of-Thought', 'Prompt Injection'], 'targets': [{'label': 'The user provides no structural behavioral examples, directly requesting a functional result.', 'answer': 'Zero-shot'}, {'label': 'The user explicitly instructs the model to break down its reasoning steps sequentially before outputting the final conclusion.', 'answer': 'Chain-of-Thought'}, {'label': 'A malicious text exploit tricking an LLM into bypassing its system safety guardrails.', 'answer': 'Prompt Injection'}], 'correct_answer': ['Zero-shot', 'Chain-of-Thought', 'Prompt Injection'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'Zero-shot includes no examples. Chain-of-thought requests sequential step-by-step logic. Prompt injection is an adversarial system exploit.', 'incorrect': 'Review core prompt engineering glossary terms.', 'concept': 'Prompt engineering terminology matching.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['zero-shot', 'cot', 'prompt-injection']},
        {'id': 'Q38', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Azure AI Language: Advanced Operations', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A security firm wants to implement an intelligent system using Azure AI Language. They want to flag customer complaints containing aggressive text behavior while automatically filtering out billing account details like credit card tokens to remain compliant with corporate handling regulations.', 'question': 'What two capabilities of Azure AI Language should they use?', 'options': ['Language Detection and Translation', 'PII Redaction and Sentiment Analysis', 'Summarization and Conversational Slot-Filling', 'Text Custom Classification and Speech-to-Text'], 'correct_answer': 'PII Redaction and Sentiment Analysis', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Sentiment Analysis can identify aggressive language trends, while PII Redaction detects and scrubs sensitive credentials dynamically.', 'incorrect': 'Translation translates. Summarization condenses. Custom classification labels files, but does not sanitize inputs or read sentiment tones out of the box in a single interface config.', 'concept': 'Azure AI Language capabilities combination.'}, 'avg_time': 60, 'confused_services': ['pii', 'sentiment']},
        {'id': 'Q39', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Generative AI: Social Hazards', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'What is a primary social hazard or threat associated with the malicious use of advanced generative AI multi-modal models?', 'question': 'Select the primary social hazard.', 'options': ['Increased storage management efficiency on edge infrastructure.', 'Creation of highly convincing deepfakes and manipulated media for disinformation.', 'Automatic reduction in public electricity consumption rates.', 'Removal of all network firewalls globally.'], 'correct_answer': 'Creation of highly convincing deepfakes and manipulated media for disinformation.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'The creation of hyper-realistic digital deepfakes, synthesized voice clips, and manipulated media is a primary societal hazard of advanced generative systems.', 'incorrect': 'Storage efficiency, power reduction, and firewall removals are not standard social hazards associated with generative AI media manipulation.', 'concept': 'Societal risks of generative AI.'}, 'avg_time': 30, 'confused_services': ['generative-ai', 'safety']},
        {'id': 'Q40', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure AI Document Intelligence: Prebuilt Receipt', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A food distribution platform needs a system to scan mobile photographs of supplier paper delivery receipts to log the vendor names, line items, and transaction dates into a database.', 'question': 'Which Azure AI service provides pre-built structures optimized for this exact workload?', 'options': ['Azure AI Face API', 'Azure AI Document Intelligence (Prebuilt Receipt Model)', 'Azure AI Speech Custom Keyword API', 'Azure OpenAI DALL-E 3'], 'correct_answer': 'Azure AI Document Intelligence (Prebuilt Receipt Model)', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Document Intelligence features an out-of-the-box Prebuilt Receipt Model explicitly optimized to extract data points like merchant names, transaction line items, and totals from receipt formats.', 'incorrect': 'Face API extracts face geometries. Speech checks voice. DALL-E generates images.', 'concept': 'Azure AI Document Intelligence prebuilt receipts.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['doc-intel', 'ocr']},
        {'id': 'Q41', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Responsible AI: Algorithmic Bias', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You observe that an AI recruiting tool consistently returns lower performance evaluation indices for candidates who list universities located in specific geographic zones, despite identical historical work backgrounds.', 'question': 'This systemic error is an operational example of what machine learning issue?', 'options': ['High model transparency', 'Algorithmic bias within the historical training data profiles', 'Over-parameterization of token indices', 'Perfect fairness optimization'], 'correct_answer': 'Algorithmic bias within the historical training data profiles', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Systematically applying lower scores to specific regional demographics due to inherited training inequalities is an objective demonstration of algorithmic data bias.', 'incorrect': 'Transparency relates to explanations. Token over-parameterization relates to context size. Perfect fairness would not show bias.', 'concept': 'Data bias in machine learning models.'}, 'avg_time': 60, 'confused_services': ['fairness', 'model-training']},
        {'id': 'Q42', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure AI Foundry: Content Filter Operations', 'type': 'true-false-matrix', 'scenario': 'For each of the following statements regarding Azure AI Content Filtering, select Yes if the statement is true, otherwise select No.', 'statements': [{'text': 'Azure AI Foundry content filters can classify and filter content across categories including hate speech, sexual content, violence, and self-harm.', 'answer': 'Yes'}, {'text': 'Content filtering can only check the incoming user prompt text, and cannot evaluate the generated text output from the model.', 'answer': 'No'}, {'text': 'Developers can adjust severity thresholds (Low, Medium, High) to control how strictly content is blocked or allowed.', 'answer': 'Yes'}], 'correct_answer': ['Yes', 'No', 'Yes'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'Content filters block hate, sexual, violence, and self-harm. Filters evaluate both incoming user prompts AND outbound model responses across adjustable severity limits (Low, Medium, High), rendering Row 2 incorrect.', 'incorrect': 'Review content filtering execution steps.', 'concept': 'Azure AI Content Filtering parameters.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['content-filtering']},
        {'id': 'Q43', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Generative AI: Fine-Tuning Models', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'Which technique involves modifying the structural weights of an existing pre-trained foundation model by training it on a smaller, highly domain-specific dataset to align its outputs with specific formatting or specialized terminology?', 'question': 'Select the correct technique term.', 'options': ['Zero-shot text prompt engineering', 'RAG indexing', 'Fine-tuning', 'Token clearing'], 'correct_answer': 'Fine-tuning', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Fine-tuning is the process of altering the actual internal weight configurations of an established model by running backpropagation using specialized secondary training datasets.', 'incorrect': 'Prompt engineering does not modify weights. RAG retrieves files at query time. Token clearing is not a model modification method.', 'concept': 'Model Fine-tuning definition.'}, 'avg_time': 35, 'confused_services': ['fine-tuning', 'rag']},
        {'id': 'Q44', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure AI Speech: transcribing phone calls', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A customer service company wants to convert live phone support recordings into textual data to perform automated audits.', 'question': 'Which Azure AI service is the MOST appropriate selection?', 'options': ['Azure AI Language', 'Azure AI Speech', 'Azure AI Vision', 'Azure AI Document Intelligence'], 'correct_answer': 'Azure AI Speech', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Converting vocal recordings and phone support audio streams into readable text files is the primary objective of Azure AI Speech (Speech-to-Text).', 'incorrect': 'Language parses text strings. Vision processes images. Document Intelligence reads invoices.', 'concept': 'Azure AI Speech workloads.'}, 'avg_time': 40, 'confused_services': ['speech', 'language']},
        {'id': 'Q45', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Responsible AI: Transparency & Accountability', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'When designing an AI system that processes mortgage loans, you decide to include a detailed explanation log that informs rejected applicants exactly which parameters (e.g., debt-to-income ratio, credit history duration) led to the negative decision.', 'question': 'This architecture adheres to which Responsible AI concept?', 'options': ['Fairness and Inclusiveness', 'Accountability and Transparency', 'Privacy and Security', 'Reliability and Safety'], 'correct_answer': 'Accountability and Transparency', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Providing clear explanations for automated decisions ensures Transparency, while keeping verifiable systemic rationale logs ensures institutional Accountability.', 'incorrect': 'Inclusiveness handles disability. Privacy concerns records. Safety involves mechanical hazards.', 'concept': 'Responsible AI principles mappings.'}, 'avg_time': 60, 'confused_services': ['transparency', 'accountability']},
        {'id': 'Q46', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure AI Language: NLP features', 'type': 'true-false-matrix', 'scenario': 'For each of the following statements regarding Natural Language Processing (NLP) workloads on Azure, select Yes if the statement is true, otherwise select No.', 'statements': [{'text': 'Key phrase extraction identifies the core conversational talking points within a massive unindexed block of text.', 'answer': 'Yes'}, {'text': 'Language detection returns a confidence numerical score indicating the primary language of a target string.', 'answer': 'Yes'}, {'text': 'Azure AI Language requires manual translation configuration before it can extract entities from Spanish or French documents.', 'answer': 'No'}], 'correct_answer': ['Yes', 'Yes', 'No'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'Key phrases extracts topics. Language detection finds translation codes and prints confidence decimals. Language natively supports multi-lingual entity extraction out-of-the-box without manual translations (rendering Row 3 false).', 'incorrect': 'Review multi-language features of Azure Language APIs.', 'concept': 'Azure AI Language NLP capabilities.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['language-translation', 'language-features']},
        {'id': 'Q47', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Prompt Engineering: Chain of Thought', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': "In generative AI prompt engineering, what is the term for explicitly telling the model to 'think step-by-step' to solve a logical puzzle or mathematical problem?", 'question': 'Select the correct prompt engineering term.', 'options': ['Negative prompting', 'Chain-of-Thought prompting', 'Zero-shot generation', 'Hyperparameter optimization'], 'correct_answer': 'Chain-of-Thought prompting', 'explanations': {'correct': "Forcing an LLM to generate its intermediate logical paths explicitly using phrases like 'think step-by-step' is the definition of Chain-of-Thought prompting.", 'incorrect': 'Negative prompting lists blocked terms. Zero-shot provides no examples. Hyperparameter tuning is deep learning configuration.', 'concept': 'Chain-of-Thought prompting.'}, 'avg_time': 30, 'confused_services': ['cot', 'few-shot']},
        {'id': 'Q48', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Azure AI Vision: Custom Model', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'An international engineering company requires a localized safety solution for its industrial facilities. The system must process live closed-circuit camera frames to detect if personnel are wearing compliant hardhats and high-visibility safety vests, throwing immediate alerts to safety managers.', 'question': 'Which service option provides the BEST baseline architecture?', 'options': ['Azure AI Language (NER)', 'Azure AI Document Intelligence (Layout model)', 'Azure AI Vision (Custom Object Detection Model)', 'Azure OpenAI Service (DALL-E 3 generation pipeline)'], 'correct_answer': 'Azure AI Vision (Custom Object Detection Model)', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Training Azure AI Vision with custom images of hardhats and safety gear to spot and tag them within live video frames implements custom object detection.', 'incorrect': 'Language parses text files. Document Intelligence reads document sheets. DALL-E generates images, it does not evaluate camera streams for object boundaries.', 'concept': 'Azure AI Vision: Custom Object Detection.'}, 'avg_time': 65, 'confused_services': ['vision', 'doc-intel']},
        {'id': 'Q49', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'AI Workloads: CV segmenting', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'Which of the following describes an example of an AI capability focused on Computer Vision?', 'question': 'Select the correct Computer Vision capability example.', 'options': ['Detecting fraudulent transaction charges from a credit log.', 'Translating a text manual from German into Japanese.', 'Segmenting an aerial drone image to locate forest fire boundaries.', 'Clustering users based on historical email response rates.'], 'correct_answer': 'Segmenting an aerial drone image to locate forest fire boundaries.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Segmenting, processing, or classifying pixels in an aerial photograph to isolate geographic boundaries is a core Computer Vision workload.', 'incorrect': 'Fraud detection is anomaly detection. Translation is NLP. User clustering is K-Means K-clustering.', 'concept': 'Computer Vision workloads.'}, 'avg_time': 30, 'confused_services': ['cv', 'nlp']},
        {'id': 'Q50', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Conversational AI: Orchestrated Agents', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A software development company is launching a conversational assistant in Azure AI Foundry. They want to ensure that the application can fetch answers from an enterprise-managed knowledge base, while dynamically keeping track of multiple sequential tool executions to verify inventory levels and update external tracking records.', 'question': 'What architectural concept does this represent?', 'options': ['Static Prompt Engineering Matrix', 'Orchestrated AI Agent with Tool Capabilities', 'Pure Image Segmentation Pipeline', 'Unsupervised Clustering Network'], 'correct_answer': 'Orchestrated AI Agent with Tool Capabilities', 'explanations': {'correct': 'An application that leverages an LLM core alongside autonomous planning, external knowledge retrieval (RAG), and sequential tool calling to query and modify databases describes an AI Agent.', 'incorrect': 'Prompt matrix is a list. Image segmentation is for graphics. K-clustering groups records.', 'concept': 'AI Agent architectures.'}, 'avg_time': 60, 'confused_services': ['chatbot', 'agent']},
        {'id': 'Q51', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Responsible AI: Matching', 'type': 'drag-drop', 'scenario': 'Match each business action with the Responsible AI principle it upholds.', 'question': 'Match the business action with the Responsible AI principle.', 'correct_answer': ['Fairness', 'Privacy & Security', 'Reliability & Safety'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'Fairness ensures equitable performance across different demographics. Privacy and Security covers encrypting data in transit (HTTPS). Reliability and Safety involves robust fail-safe mechanics for hardware failures.', 'incorrect': "Ensure you don't confuse data privacy safeguards with algorithmic bias prevention or physical safety protocols.", 'concept': 'Responsible AI principles matching.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['fairness', 'privacy-security', 'reliability'], 'draggableItems': ['Fairness', 'Privacy & Security', 'Reliability & Safety'], 'targets': [{'label': 'Testing facial recognition across diverse ethnic group data.', 'answer': 'Fairness'}, {'label': 'Enforcing HTTPS encryption on diagnostic transcripts.', 'answer': 'Privacy & Security'}, {'label': 'Configuring automatic fail-safes if obstacle sensors report errors.', 'answer': 'Reliability & Safety'}]},
        {'id': 'Q52', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Responsible AI: Hotspot Selector', 'type': 'dropdown-hotspot', 'scenario': 'Select the correct principles based on the scenarios.', 'question': 'Select the correct principle from the dropdown options.', 'correct_answer': ['Fairness', 'Transparency'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'Inclusiveness ensures system accessibility for users of all abilities. Accountability demands operational oversight and auditing framework, whereas Transparency deals with system explainability and disclosure, not shifting sole liability without human oversight.', 'incorrect': 'Transparency does not eliminate accountability or assign legal liability automatically.', 'concept': 'Responsible AI standards.'}, 'avg_time': 40, 'confused_services': ['fairness', 'transparency'], 'parts': [{'text': 'Ensuring a model does not discriminate by age supports ', 'options': ['Fairness', 'Inclusiveness', 'Accountability'], 'answer': 'Fairness'}, {'text': '. Ensuring that users know they are chatting with a bot supports ', 'options': ['Transparency', 'Reliability & Safety', 'Privacy & Security'], 'answer': 'Transparency'}]},
        {'id': 'Q53', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Responsible AI: Basic definitions', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': "You are training your team on Responsible AI. You want to summarize what 'Accountability' represents in a single phrase.", 'question': 'Which of the following BEST defines Accountability?', 'correct_answer': 'Ensuring humans are answerable for the operation and outcomes of AI systems.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Accountability focuses on establishing human responsibility and answerability for AI systems.', 'incorrect': 'Encryption relates to Privacy. Accessibility relates to Inclusiveness. Explaining weights relates to Transparency.', 'concept': 'Accountability definition.'}, 'avg_time': 30, 'confused_services': ['accountability', 'transparency'], 'options': ['Encrypting user data to prevent leakage.', 'Ensuring humans are answerable for the operation and outcomes of AI systems.', 'Making chatbots accessible to blind users.', 'Explaining the mathematical weights of neural networks.']},
        {'id': 'Q54', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Responsible AI: Security threat model', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A bank deploying a customer loan assistant wants to prevent adversarial attacks where hackers feed malicious inputs to force the AI to dump private client databases.', 'question': 'Which principle handles this risk?', 'correct_answer': 'Privacy and Security', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Preventing adversarial attacks and securing databases is a core objective of Privacy and Security.', 'incorrect': 'Inclusiveness, Fairness, and Transparency focus on accessibility, non-discrimination, and explainability respectively.', 'concept': 'Security vulnerabilities and risk management.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['privacy-security', 'transparency'], 'options': ['Privacy and Security', 'Inclusiveness', 'Fairness', 'Transparency']},
        {'id': 'Q55', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Responsible AI: Safety fail-safes', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': "An AI diagnostic system deployed in a hospital operates correctly in 99% of cases, but in 1% of cases it fails to read scans due to corruption. The developer adds a rule: 'If image quality is low, route the scan immediately to a human doctor.'", 'question': 'Which principle is supported by this fallback rule?', 'correct_answer': 'Reliability and Safety', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Implementing human fallback loops for low-confidence or corrupted inputs maintains operational safety and prevents harm, supporting Reliability and Safety.', 'incorrect': 'Accessibility (Inclusiveness), bias mitigation (Fairness), and explanations (Transparency) do not directly cover mechanical human fallbacks.', 'concept': 'Fail-safes and human-in-the-loop validation.'}, 'avg_time': 55, 'confused_services': ['reliability', 'transparency'], 'options': ['Reliability and Safety', 'Inclusiveness', 'Fairness', 'Transparency']},
        {'id': 'Q56', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'AI Workloads: CV Capabilities', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': "A design team wants to upload sketches and have the system automatically tag objects like 'chair', 'table', and 'window' in each sketch.", 'question': 'Which AI workload matches this feature?', 'correct_answer': 'Computer Vision (Image Analysis)', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Tagging visual elements in images (like chairs or tables) is a core capability of Image Analysis in Computer Vision.', 'incorrect': 'NER parses text. Speech translation handles audio. Regression predicts numbers.', 'concept': 'Image analysis tagging capabilities.'}, 'avg_time': 30, 'confused_services': ['cv', 'ner'], 'options': ['Named Entity Recognition', 'Computer Vision (Image Analysis)', 'Speech Translation', 'Regression']},
        {'id': 'Q57', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'AI Workloads: Speech Translation', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A tourism agency wants a mobile app where a user can speak in Japanese, and the phone speaks back the English translation.', 'question': 'Which AI workload is required?', 'correct_answer': 'Speech Translation', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Speech Translation converts spoken audio directly to text or speech in another language.', 'incorrect': 'Sentiment is text tone. OCR reads characters. Object detection locates visual items.', 'concept': 'Speech-to-speech translation workloads.'}, 'avg_time': 30, 'confused_services': ['speech-translation', 'translation'], 'options': ['Natural Language Processing Sentiment Analysis', 'Speech Translation', 'OCR', 'Object Detection']},
        {'id': 'Q58', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Generative AI: Summarization', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A firm wants to ingest 500-page board meeting transcripts and produce a bulleted 1-page action plan summarizing the decisions.', 'question': 'Which AI capability is MOST appropriate?', 'correct_answer': 'Generative AI Text Summarization', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Generative AI text models excel at parsing large texts and summarizing semantic context.', 'incorrect': 'NER extracts entities but does not synthesize summaries. OCR reads print characters. Regression forecasts numbers.', 'concept': 'Summarization capabilities of foundation models.'}, 'avg_time': 40, 'confused_services': ['summarization', 'ner'], 'options': ['Named Entity Recognition', 'Generative AI Text Summarization', 'Optical Character Recognition', 'Regression Forecasting']},
        {'id': 'Q59', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'AI Workloads: Sentiment Analysis', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A restaurant chain wants to monitor social media posts containing their name and flag posts that express positive, neutral, or negative customer experiences.', 'question': 'Which NLP capability is MOST appropriate?', 'correct_answer': 'Sentiment Analysis', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Sentiment Analysis analyzes text and outputs scores representing the tone or attitude (positive/negative/neutral).', 'incorrect': 'NER extracts tags. Translation changes language. Summarization condenses blocks.', 'concept': 'Sentiment classification in text processing.'}, 'avg_time': 35, 'confused_services': ['sentiment', 'ner'], 'options': ['Named Entity Recognition', 'Sentiment Analysis', 'Translation', 'Summarization']},
        {'id': 'Q60', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'AI Workloads: Face detection', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'An art exhibition wants to count the number of visitors and estimate their age range and gender based on camera feeds at the entrance, without storing individual face signatures.', 'question': 'Which capability should they use?', 'correct_answer': 'Face Analysis (detection & attributes)', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Face detection and attribute estimation can evaluate age and gender from faces without registering or storing biometric identification signatures.', 'incorrect': "OCR reads text. Object detection boxes items. Spatial analysis tracks crowds but doesn't evaluate facial attributes.", 'concept': 'Facial detection vs. biometric facial recognition identification.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['face-api', 'spatial-analysis'], 'options': ['Optical Character Recognition', 'Face Analysis (detection & attributes)', 'Object Detection bounding boxes', 'Spatial Analysis queue tracking']},
        {'id': 'Q61', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Generative AI: Code generation capabilities', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A software company wants their developers to use an AI that suggests whole functions in Python, formats SQL syntax, and checks code for security exploits.', 'question': 'Which class of model provides these capabilities natively?', 'correct_answer': 'A Large Language Model pre-trained on text and source code repositories', 'explanations': {'correct': 'LLMs pre-trained on code (like GPT-4 or Codex series) contain structural code generation, reasoning, and correction capabilities.', 'incorrect': 'Regression, vision, and clustering networks do not possess text/code syntax generation capabilities.', 'concept': 'Code intelligence capabilities of foundation LLMs.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['llms', 'model-training'], 'options': ['A standard regression network', 'A Large Language Model pre-trained on text and source code repositories', 'A computer vision segmentation network', 'A clustering partition network']},
        {'id': 'Q62', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Generative AI: Vision LLM capabilities', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': "You want to build an AI system for blind users. A user can upload a photo of a restaurant menu, and the AI should read the menu, understand the user's spoken question (e.g. 'Is there vegetarian soup?'), and speak back the answer.", 'question': 'Which combination of capabilities is MOST appropriate?', 'correct_answer': 'Multimodal Generative AI (Vision-to-Text), Speech-to-Text, and Text-to-Speech', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Parsing the menu photo requires Vision-to-Text (Multimodal LLM). Understanding questions requires Speech-to-Text, and replying requires Text-to-Speech.', 'incorrect': 'Anomaly detection, image classification, and clustering do not address multimodal question answering or vocal speech conversions.', 'concept': 'Multimodal generative AI applications.'}, 'avg_time': 60, 'confused_services': ['vision', 'speech', 'multimodal'], 'options': ['Multimodal Generative AI (Vision-to-Text), Speech-to-Text, and Text-to-Speech', 'Pure OCR, and Anomaly Detection', 'Image classification, and translation', 'Clustering, and text-to-speech']},
        {'id': 'Q63', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Generative AI: Workload matrix', 'type': 'true-false-matrix', 'scenario': 'For each of the following statements about AI model capabilities, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.', 'question': 'Select the correct option for each statement.', 'correct_answer': ['Yes', 'No', 'Yes'], 'explanations': {'correct': "Temperature is a continuous number, so predicting it requires a Regression model. Email categories ('Spam' vs 'Inbox') are discrete labels, which requires a Classification model.", 'incorrect': 'Clustering is for unsupervised grouping. Regression does not sort categories.', 'concept': 'Regression vs Classification workloads.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['generative-ai', 'regression', 'speech'], 'statements': [{'text': 'Generative AI models can generate realistic synthetic images from text.', 'answer': 'Yes'}, {'text': 'A standard regression model can generate natural conversational responses.', 'answer': 'No'}, {'text': 'Text-to-Speech converts written scripts into audio vocalizations.', 'answer': 'Yes'}]},
        {'id': 'Q64', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Generative AI: Workload matching', 'type': 'drag-drop', 'scenario': 'Match each customer requirement with the most suitable AI model capability.', 'question': 'Match the requirement with the model capability.', 'correct_answer': ['Text Translation', 'Image Generation', 'Sentiment Classification'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'Text translation handles language translation. Image generation creates novel imagery from text descriptions. Sentiment classification categorizes reviews based on emotional tone.', 'incorrect': 'Ensure you map language translation, image synthesis, and emotion tagging to the correct capabilities.', 'concept': 'Generative AI workload capabilities.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['translation', 'image-generation', 'sentiment'], 'draggableItems': ['Text Translation', 'Image Generation', 'Sentiment Classification'], 'targets': [{'label': 'Translating user comments from German to English.', 'answer': 'Text Translation'}, {'label': 'Creating mockups of logo ideas based on descriptions.', 'answer': 'Image Generation'}, {'label': 'Tagging reviews as happy or unhappy.', 'answer': 'Sentiment Classification'}]},
        {'id': 'Q65', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Generative AI: Capability limits', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': "You deploy a standard generative AI chatbot. A customer asks: 'Will stock price ABC increase tomorrow?' The model replies: 'I cannot predict future stock movements.'", 'question': "What is the primary technical reason for the model's reply?", 'correct_answer': 'The model is a statistical text generator that lacks real-time future prediction capabilities.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Generative language models produce text based on historical training data; they cannot predict future real-world events or generate facts about the future.', 'incorrect': 'Models are probabilistic, not deterministic. Temperature settings and SQL conversions do not grant predictive future vision.', 'concept': 'Generative model limitations in future forecasting.'}, 'avg_time': 55, 'confused_services': ['generative-ai', 'regression'], 'options': ['The model is a deterministic system that cannot process probability.', 'The model is a statistical text generator that lacks real-time future prediction capabilities.', "The model's temperature parameter is set to 0.0.", 'The user must translate the prompt to SQL first.']},
        {'id': 'Q66', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Azure AI Foundry: Hubs vs Projects', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You are setting up Azure AI Foundry. You need to create a parent resource that defines the security perimeter, manages billing scopes, and configures connections to data sources.', 'question': 'Which resource should you create FIRST?', 'correct_answer': 'Azure AI Hub', 'explanations': {'correct': 'An Azure AI Hub is the parent resource that handles enterprise governance, billing, security, and connections across projects.', 'incorrect': 'An Azure AI Project is a child resource where development occurs. Deployments and compute nodes are created inside projects.', 'concept': 'Azure AI Foundry structural hierarchies.'}, 'avg_time': 40, 'confused_services': ['hub', 'project'], 'options': ['Azure AI Project', 'Azure AI Hub', 'Model Deployment', 'Compute Node']},
        {'id': 'Q67', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Azure AI Foundry: Projects', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'Your developers need an isolated collaborative environment in Azure AI Foundry to test models, write prompts, and compile evaluation logs.', 'question': 'What resource type must be configured inside the AI Hub for this work?', 'correct_answer': 'Azure AI Project', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Projects are developer workspaces created inside Hubs for deploying models and running tasks.', 'incorrect': 'Model catalog is the model repository. Compute nodes provide power but not project boundaries. Billing scopes manage costs.', 'concept': 'Azure AI Projects represent development spaces.'}, 'avg_time': 35, 'confused_services': ['hub', 'project'], 'options': ['Azure AI Project', 'Model Catalog', 'Shared Compute Node', 'Billing scope']},
        {'id': 'Q68', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Azure OpenAI: Model Catalog', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You are configuring a deployment in Azure OpenAI. You need a model that can perform text completion, coding support, and multi-modal image reading.', 'question': 'Which model should you select?', 'correct_answer': 'GPT-4o', 'explanations': {'correct': 'GPT-4o is the multimodal conversational model family supporting text, code, and images.', 'incorrect': 'Text-Embedding generates vectors. DALL-E generates images from text. Whisper transcribes audio.', 'concept': 'Azure OpenAI model catalog families.'}, 'avg_time': 35, 'confused_services': ['gpt-4o', 'dall-e'], 'options': ['Text-Embedding-3', 'GPT-4o', 'DALL-E 3', 'Whisper']},
        {'id': 'Q69', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Azure OpenAI: Content Filtering', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You deploy an Azure OpenAI model. You want to automatically block user inputs containing explicit violence or self-harm before they reach the model.', 'question': 'Which Azure OpenAI feature provides this safety filter?', 'correct_answer': 'Content Filtering', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Azure OpenAI Content Filtering evaluates inputs and outputs against harm categories to block unsafe items.', 'incorrect': 'Prompt flow manages workflows. System prompts instruct behavior. Fine-tuning adjusts weights.', 'concept': 'Content Filtering acts as the automated safety gate.'}, 'avg_time': 30, 'confused_services': ['content-filtering', 'system-prompt'], 'options': ['Prompt Flow', 'Content Filtering', 'System Prompts', 'Model Fine-Tuning']},
        {'id': 'Q70', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Azure OpenAI: Fine-Tuning', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You want to deploy an Azure OpenAI model, but you need to adapt the model parameters so that it uses a highly specialized engineering vocabulary.', 'question': 'Which model adaptation technique should you execute?', 'correct_answer': 'Model Fine-Tuning', 'explanations': {'correct': "Fine-tuning updates a base model's weights on a custom dataset, training it in specific vocabulary and styles.", 'incorrect': 'RAG injects text at runtime. Zero-shot is a prompt style. Temperature controls randomness.', 'concept': 'Fine-tuning updates model weights.'}, 'avg_time': 40, 'confused_services': ['fine-tuning', 'rag'], 'options': ['Retrieval-Augmented Generation', 'Model Fine-Tuning', 'Zero-shot prompting', 'Increasing temperature']},
        {'id': 'Q71', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure OpenAI: Custom Blocklists', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': "A bank wants to block customers from typing their competitors' names (e.g. 'BankA', 'BankB') in their Azure OpenAI chatbot.", 'question': 'What is the RECOMMENDED implementation method?', 'correct_answer': 'Create a custom blocklist containing the competitor names inside Azure OpenAI Content Filtering, and apply it to the model deployment.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Custom blocklists in Content Filtering detect and block exact term matches in inputs and outputs.', 'incorrect': 'Standard filters target general harm (hate, sexual), not business-specific terms. System prompts can fail to block terms consistently. Temperature is for variance.', 'concept': 'Custom blocklists support corporate safety policies.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['content-filtering', 'blocklist'], 'options': ['Set Content Filtering hate speech thresholds to High.', 'Create a custom blocklist containing the competitor names inside Azure OpenAI Content Filtering, and apply it to the model deployment.', 'Write a 10-page System Prompt listing all banking terms.', 'Increase the temperature parameter to 1.0.']},
        {'id': 'Q72', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure OpenAI: Deployment Options', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You are deploying a customer assistant. You want a deployment that charges you strictly for the number of input and output tokens processed, with no dedicated throughput guarantees.', 'question': 'Which deployment type should you select?', 'correct_answer': 'Standard (Pay-As-You-Go)', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Standard (Pay-As-You-Go) deployments bill based on token usage volume, perfect for variable workloads.', 'incorrect': 'PTU guarantees throughput but charges a fixed rate for provisioned capacity. Local containers and reserved instances are not standard pay-per-token Azure OpenAI models.', 'concept': 'Deployment pricing models.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['ptu', 'standard'], 'options': ['Provisioned Throughput (PTU)', 'Standard (Pay-As-You-Go)', 'Local container', 'Reserved instance']},
        {'id': 'Q73', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure AI Foundry: Model Catalog', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You want to evaluate and compare open-source foundation models (such as Llama-3 or Mistral) alongside Azure OpenAI models inside Azure AI Foundry.', 'question': 'Which feature of the Foundry interface contains this library of models?', 'correct_answer': 'Model Catalog', 'explanations': {'correct': 'The Model Catalog contains a collection of Microsoft, OpenAI, and open-source models for comparison and deployment.', 'incorrect': 'Prompt flow is for workflows. Connections link data resources. Content filters manage safety.', 'concept': 'Model Catalog is a unified repository of models.'}, 'avg_time': 40, 'confused_services': ['model-catalog', 'connections'], 'options': ['Prompt Flow', 'Model Catalog', 'Azure AI Hub connections', 'Content Filters']},
        {'id': 'Q74', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Azure OpenAI: Content Filtering severity thresholds', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You want to restrict your model from outputting minor instances of hate speech, but you want to ensure it does not block benign queries that discuss clinical terms.', 'question': 'How should you adjust the severity thresholds for content filters?', 'correct_answer': 'Set the filter action threshold to Low to block low-severity entries, or Medium for standard filtering.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Setting the threshold to Low/Medium blocks content starting at those low/medium severity levels. Setting it to High only blocks extreme risk, letting mild items pass.', 'incorrect': 'Setting the block threshold to High means you allow low/medium risk content to pass, which is less restrictive.', 'concept': 'Content Filter severity thresholds configuration.'}, 'avg_time': 55, 'confused_services': ['content-filtering-thresholds'], 'options': ['Set the filter action threshold to Low to block low-severity entries, or Medium for standard filtering.', 'Set the filter action threshold to High to maximize safety.', 'Set the temperature to 0.0.', 'Disable inputs content filters and only filter outputs.']},
        {'id': 'Q75', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Azure AI Foundry: Shared Compute Hub', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You are a cloud architect setting up Azure AI Foundry. You need to enforce data security policies (such as Private Endpoints) that automatically apply to all child projects created by five separate development teams.', 'question': 'Where should you configure these network security policies?', 'correct_answer': 'In the parent Azure AI Hub', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Configuring security, networking, and endpoints on the parent Hub ensures they are inherited by all child projects automatically.', 'incorrect': 'Configuring per project leads to duplication. Model catalog and databases do not manage workspace-wide virtual networks.', 'concept': 'Hub governance and security inheritance.'}, 'avg_time': 60, 'confused_services': ['hub', 'project'], 'options': ['In each individual Project', 'In the parent Azure AI Hub', 'In the Model Catalog deployment settings', 'In the SQL Database connector properties']},
        {'id': 'Q76', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure OpenAI: True/False Matrix', 'type': 'true-false-matrix', 'scenario': 'For each of the following statements about Azure OpenAI services, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.', 'question': 'Select the correct option for each statement.', 'correct_answer': ['Yes', 'No', 'Yes'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'System messages establish core persona guidelines and behavioral bounds. Lowering temperature reduces output variation and increases determinism. Deploying custom content filtering rules in Azure OpenAI requires Microsoft modification approval.', 'incorrect': 'Increasing temperature makes outputs more creative/random, not deterministic.', 'concept': 'Azure OpenAI deployment and parameters.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['fine-tuning', 'gpt-4o', 'content-filtering'], 'statements': [{'text': 'Azure OpenAI models can be customized using Fine-Tuning inside Azure AI Studio.', 'answer': 'Yes'}, {'text': 'GPT-4o is only capable of processing text inputs.', 'answer': 'No'}, {'text': 'Content Filtering is enabled by default for all Azure OpenAI deployments.', 'answer': 'Yes'}]},
        {'id': 'Q77', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure OpenAI: Matching', 'type': 'drag-drop', 'scenario': 'Match each Azure OpenAI model family with its primary capability.', 'question': 'Match the model family with the primary capability.', 'correct_answer': ['Text-Embedding-3', 'GPT-4o', 'Whisper'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'Text-Embedding-3 creates high-dimensional vector representations. GPT-4o conducts multi-modal chat conversations. Whisper transcribes speech audio into text.', 'incorrect': 'Do not confuse text embeddings with conversational models or audio transcribers.', 'concept': 'Azure OpenAI model capabilities.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['embeddings', 'gpt-4o', 'whisper'], 'draggableItems': ['GPT-4o', 'Text-Embedding-3', 'Whisper'], 'targets': [{'label': 'Generating vector floats representing textual meaning.', 'answer': 'Text-Embedding-3'}, {'label': 'Conducting multi-modal conversations.', 'answer': 'GPT-4o'}, {'label': 'Transcribing audio recordings to text.', 'answer': 'Whisper'}]},
        {'id': 'Q78', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Azure AI Foundry: Studio Portal', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A business analyst wants to test prompt completions and configure model settings in a web-based portal interface without writing python code.', 'question': 'Which tool or portal provides this graphic playground?', 'correct_answer': 'Azure AI Foundry portal (Studio)', 'explanations': {'correct': 'The Azure AI Foundry portal provides developers and analysts with visual playgrounds, prompt design boxes, and catalog deployment controls.', 'incorrect': 'Azure Portal handles infrastructure resources. CLI is code command-line. Storage explorer is for database file browsing.', 'concept': 'Azure AI Studio/Foundry portals facilitate graphic configurations.'}, 'avg_time': 30, 'confused_services': ['studio', 'azure-portal'], 'options': ['Azure Portal Resource Manager', 'Azure AI Foundry portal (Studio)', 'Azure CLI terminal', 'Azure Storage Explorer']},
        {'id': 'Q79', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Azure AI Vision: OCR', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A school needs to scan photos of printed signboards and retrieve the text content from the photos.', 'question': 'Which Azure AI Vision capability is MOST appropriate?', 'correct_answer': 'Optical Character Recognition (OCR)', 'explanations': {'correct': 'OCR is the capability designed to extract printed or handwritten text characters from images.', 'incorrect': 'Object detection returns bounding boxes. Face API detects faces. Spatial analysis tracks movement streams.', 'concept': 'OCR text extraction from raster graphics.'}, 'avg_time': 35, 'confused_services': ['ocr', 'object-detection'], 'options': ['Image Analysis (Object Detection)', 'Optical Character Recognition (OCR)', 'Face API', 'Spatial Analysis']},
        {'id': 'Q80', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Azure AI Document Intelligence: Prebuilt receipt', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'An accounting firm wants to scan photos of sales receipts and extract transaction amounts, merchant names, and tax totals automatically, with MINIMUM effort.', 'question': 'Which Azure service should they deploy?', 'correct_answer': 'Azure AI Document Intelligence (Prebuilt Receipt model)', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Document Intelligence prebuilt models are designed to recognize receipt formats and return mapped key-value pairs (like merchant, totals) out of the box.', 'incorrect': 'Generic OCR only dumps raw text strings without structured semantic key mapping. Language parses text inputs. Face API handles faces.', 'concept': 'Prebuilt Document Intelligence models map standard layouts.'}, 'avg_time': 40, 'confused_services': ['doc-intel', 'ocr'], 'options': ['Azure AI Vision OCR', 'Azure AI Document Intelligence (Prebuilt Receipt model)', 'Azure AI Language', 'Face API']},
        {'id': 'Q81', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Azure AI Vision: Image Analysis', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': "A real estate website wants to automatically scan uploaded property photos, verify that they do not contain mature content, and tag subjects like 'kitchen' or 'garden'.", 'question': 'Which service matches these requirements?', 'correct_answer': 'Azure AI Vision (Image Analysis)', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Image Analysis tags subjects, analyzes content safety (mature content), and generates descriptions.', 'incorrect': 'Document intelligence handles paper templates. Language handles text documents. Face API checks biometric attributes.', 'concept': 'Image Analysis capabilities: tagging, content moderation.'}, 'avg_time': 35, 'confused_services': ['image-analysis', 'doc-intel'], 'options': ['Azure AI Document Intelligence', 'Azure AI Vision (Image Analysis)', 'Azure AI Language', 'Face API']},
        {'id': 'Q82', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure AI Vision: Spatial Analysis', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A museum wants to analyze a live camera feed above an exhibit. They need to count how many people cross a line on the floor, and track how long they remain near the artwork.', 'question': 'Which Azure service capability should they implement?', 'correct_answer': 'Azure AI Vision (Spatial Analysis)', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Spatial Analysis tracks people movement, counts line-crossings, and measures dwell times in live video feeds.', 'incorrect': 'Document intelligence reads paper. Face verification matches identity. Language parses text strings.', 'concept': 'Spatial Analysis tracks presence and movements in video feeds.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['spatial-analysis', 'face'], 'options': ['Azure AI Vision (Spatial Analysis)', 'Azure AI Document Intelligence', 'Face API Face Verification', 'Azure AI Language']},
        {'id': 'Q83', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure AI Document Intelligence: Layout model', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You need to extract structured tables from PDF files. The tables contain multiple merged columns and variable row heights. You want to preserve the table structure in the JSON output.', 'question': 'Which Document Intelligence model is BEST?', 'correct_answer': 'Layout model', 'explanations': {'correct': 'The Layout model extracts text layout, selection marks, and structured table hierarchies from document files.', 'incorrect': 'Read model only retrieves raw text lines. Custom classifier categorizes document classes. Invoice model targets invoice templates, not arbitrary tabular reports.', 'concept': 'Layout model extracts structured tables.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['layout-model', 'read-model'], 'options': ['Prebuilt Read model', 'Layout model', 'Custom Classifier model', 'Prebuilt Invoice model']},
