        {'id': 'Q105', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'RAG: Vector Search', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': "A customer searches: 'Why is my screen blue?' In a technical help database, a standard keyword search fails, but vector search returns articles about 'graphics drivers' and 'OS recovery'.", 'question': 'Why did the vector search succeed?', 'correct_answer': 'Vector search matches semantic concept vectors rather than exact text strings.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Vector search evaluates mathematical distance in semantic vector spaces, finding concepts related to queries even when spellings differ.', 'incorrect': 'Keyword search handles characters. Vector search does not train/fine-tune models or execute standard SQL joins.', 'concept': 'Vector search matches conceptual proximity.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['vector-search', 'keyword-search'], 'options': ['Vector search matches semantic concept vectors rather than exact text strings.', "Vector search matches exact character strings like 'blue'.", 'Vector search dynamically fine-tunes the LLM.', 'Vector search executes SQL joins.']},
