        {'id': 'Q141', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Responsible AI: Security vs Transparency tradeoffs', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'To prove they are compliant with security laws, a bank wants to publish the exact prompts and validation checks used in their fraud detection engine. However, doing so would allow fraudsters to bypass the rules.', 'question': 'Which principle balance is in question?', 'correct_answer': 'Transparency vs Privacy and Security', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Publishing rules to support Transparency can introduce security exploits, violating the Security principle.', 'incorrect': 'Fairness, reliability, and inclusiveness are not directly in conflict here.', 'concept': 'Security vs transparency limits.'}, 'avg_time': 60, 'confused_services': ['transparency', 'privacy-security'], 'options': ['Transparency vs Privacy and Security', 'Fairness vs Reliability and Safety', 'Accountability vs Inclusiveness', 'Inclusiveness vs Fairness']},
        {'id': 'Q142', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Generative AI: RAG vs Fine-tuning tradeoffs', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You want to build a customer assistant that checks real-time seat numbers on trains. The seat occupancy changes every minute. You want to implement this on a minimal budget.', 'question': 'Which design approach is MOST appropriate?', 'correct_answer': 'Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) that queries the train database at query time.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'RAG queries the live database and inserts the current status in the prompt, making it suitable for real-time data changes.', 'incorrect': 'Fine-tuning every minute is computationally impossible and expensive. Regression predicts general numbers, not specific seat reservations. Filtering does not affect data queries.', 'concept': 'RAG handles dynamic runtime contexts.'}, 'avg_time': 70, 'confused_services': ['rag', 'fine-tuning'], 'options': ['Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) that queries the train database at query time.', 'Fine-tune the model parameters every minute.', 'Deploy a regression model to forecast seat numbers.', 'Disable all content filters.']},
        {'id': 'Q143', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Azure OpenAI: Custom blocklist implementations', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': "A health firm wants to block model inputs that contain terms related to competitive health plans (e.g. 'PlanX', 'PlanY').", 'question': 'How should this block be configured?', 'correct_answer': 'Configure a custom blocklist in Azure OpenAI Content Filtering.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Custom blocklists match exact custom terms in the safety filter block.', 'incorrect': 'Hate speech filters do not know corporate competitor terms. Temperature limits randomness. Embeddings are for vector matching.', 'concept': 'Custom blocklists in content filtering.'}, 'avg_time': 60, 'confused_services': ['content-filtering', 'blocklist'], 'options': ['Configure a custom blocklist in Azure OpenAI Content Filtering.', 'Set the hate speech threshold to High.', 'Set the temperature to 0.0.', 'Re-generate embeddings.']},
        {'id': 'Q144', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Azure AI Vision vs Document Intelligence selection', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A warehouse operator needs to read hand-written labels on boxes (which vary in position and layout) and structured invoice sheets (which follow a standard table layout).', 'question': 'Which combination of services is recommended?', 'correct_answer': 'Azure AI Vision OCR for the boxes, and Azure AI Document Intelligence for the invoices.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Handwritten labels on packages require generic OCR text scanning. Structured invoices are best processed by Document Intelligence to map fields.', 'incorrect': 'Document intelligence cannot scan packages easily. General vision OCR does not map invoice tables to JSON fields automatically without template logic.', 'concept': 'Selecting OCR vs. Document Intelligence.'}, 'avg_time': 65, 'confused_services': ['vision', 'doc-intel'], 'options': ['Azure AI Vision OCR for the boxes, and Azure AI Document Intelligence for the invoices.', 'Document Intelligence for all tasks.', 'Azure AI Vision Image analysis for all tasks.', 'Speech Translation for all tasks.']},
        {'id': 'Q145', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'RAG: Semantic search ranking configurations', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A medical RAG tool uses vector search but occasionally returns articles that contain the search words in incorrect contexts. You need to improve relevance with minimal latency impact.', 'question': 'Which Azure AI Search configuration is RECOMMENDED?', 'correct_answer': 'Enable the Semantic Ranker on your search index.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'The Semantic Ranker runs a secondary L2 ranking step on the top vector results using semantic matching, improving search precision.', 'incorrect': 'Pure keywords ignore conceptual relationships. Temperature is not an index configuration. Re-generating embeddings daily does not correct context matching if the model dimensions are already static.', 'concept': 'Semantic Rankers improve retrieval precision.'}, 'avg_time': 65, 'confused_services': ['semantic-ranker', 'vector-search'], 'options': ['Enable the Semantic Ranker on your search index.', 'Disable vector search and use pure keyword matches.', 'Increase the temperature parameter.', 'Re-generate embeddings daily.']},
        {'id': 'Q146', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Azure AI Foundry: Prompt Flow orchestrations', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You want to design a workflow that takes customer reviews, calls a Translation API, sends the translation to a GPT-4 model, checks the output against content filters, and updates a database.', 'question': 'Which tool provides visual orchestration and verification tests?', 'correct_answer': 'Prompt Flow', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Prompt Flow visually diagrams, tests, and evaluates multi-step generative workflows.', 'incorrect': 'Model catalog lists models. Hub handles connectivity/billing. PTU is a pricing plan.', 'concept': 'Prompt Flow orchestrates pipelines.'}, 'avg_time': 60, 'confused_services': ['prompt-flow', 'agents'], 'options': ['Prompt Flow', 'Model Catalog', 'Shared parent Hub', 'Provisioned Throughput']},
        {'id': 'Q147', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Azure OpenAI: PTU deployment calculations', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'An enterprise wants to deploy an AI system with guaranteed latency and isolated throughput capacity.', 'question': 'Which deployment option should they choose?', 'correct_answer': 'Provisioned Throughput (PTU)', 'explanations': {'correct': 'PTU guarantees dedicated model capacity, offering predictable throughput and latency.', 'incorrect': 'Standard is shared capacity (latencies can fluctuate). Local containers and Serverless do not guarantee dedicated cloud throughput.', 'concept': 'Dedicated PTU capacity deployments.'}, 'avg_time': 60, 'confused_services': ['ptu', 'standard'], 'options': ['Provisioned Throughput (PTU)', 'Standard (Pay-As-You-Go)', 'Local Docker Container', 'Serverless API']},
        {'id': 'Q148', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Foundational Python Examples: Document intelligence SDK', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': "Review this Python code: \n`poller = client.begin_analyze_document('prebuilt-invoice', document=stream)\nresult = poller.result()`", 'question': 'What happens when `poller.result()` is executed?', 'correct_answer': 'The code blocks execution and waits until the asynchronous analysis completes, returning the results.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Calling `.result()` on the poller is a blocking call that waits for the asynchronous cloud job to complete and returns the parsed data.', 'incorrect': 'It does not raise errors, open local GUIs, or delete files.', 'concept': 'Synchronous waiting on async pollers.'}, 'avg_time': 60, 'confused_services': ['async-polling', 'synch-call'], 'options': ['The code blocks execution and waits until the asynchronous analysis completes, returning the results.', 'The code exits immediately with an error.', 'The code launches a local GUI.', 'The document is deleted.']},
        {'id': 'Q149', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Azure OpenAI: Content filtering bypasses', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A company wants to completely disable all default Content Filtering for their Azure OpenAI model because they are processing highly sensitive, encrypted historical texts that trigger false positives.', 'question': 'What is required to accomplish this?', 'correct_answer': 'They must submit a formal modification request to Microsoft and obtain approval for custom safety configurations.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Disabling or fully modifying default content filtering requires submitting a request to Microsoft to ensure responsible AI practices.', 'incorrect': 'Default filters cannot be fully disabled in the GUI without Microsoft approval. Temperature and PTU instances do not bypass safety reviews.', 'concept': 'Regulated safety bypass permissions in Azure OpenAI.'}, 'avg_time': 65, 'confused_services': ['content-filtering', 'approval'], 'options': ['They must submit a formal modification request to Microsoft and obtain approval for custom safety configurations.', 'They can disable the filters directly in the Azure AI Studio GUI without approval.', 'They must set the temperature to 1.0.', 'They must buy a PTU instance.']},
        {'id': 'Q150', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Generative AI apps: True/False Matrix', 'type': 'true-false-matrix', 'scenario': 'For each of the following statements about Azure AI search integrations, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.', 'question': 'Select the correct option for each statement.', 'correct_answer': ['Yes', 'Yes', 'No'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'Semantic rankers improve search precision by using semantic logic to re-rank top hits. Hybrid search combines keywords with vector metrics. Vector search maps texts/images into floats; it does not translate databases to audio files.', 'incorrect': 'Vector indexing does not involve speech synthesis or audio conversion.', 'concept': 'Azure AI Search integrations.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['semantic-ranker', 'hybrid-search', 'vector-search'], 'statements': [{'text': 'Semantic rankers improve precision by reranking top results using semantic values.', 'answer': 'Yes'}, {'text': 'Hybrid search combines vector search with traditional keyword search.', 'answer': 'Yes'}, {'text': 'Vector search requires translating all database files into audio format.', 'answer': 'No'}]},
        {'id': 'Q151', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure AI Speech: Matching', 'type': 'drag-drop', 'scenario': 'Match each business goal with the corresponding Azure Speech capability.', 'question': 'Match the goal with the Speech capability.', 'correct_answer': ['Speaker Diarization', 'SSML tags', 'Custom Neural Voice'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'Speaker Diarization identifies who said what in a transcript. SSML tags customize pauses, pitch, and rates in voice synthesis. Custom Neural Voice builds a unique synthetic voice profile for branding.', 'incorrect': 'Diarization distinguishes speaker voices; SSML adjusts synthesis characteristics.', 'concept': 'Azure Speech features.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['diarization', 'ssml', 'neural-voice'], 'draggableItems': ['Custom Neural Voice', 'Speaker Diarization', 'SSML tags'], 'targets': [{'label': 'Distinguishing between speaker voices in a transcript.', 'answer': 'Speaker Diarization'}, {'label': 'Customizing pauses and pitch in voice synthesis.', 'answer': 'SSML tags'}, {'label': 'Creating a signature voice profile for a virtual character.', 'answer': 'Custom Neural Voice'}]},
        {'id': 'Q152', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'RAG: Search Chunking & Indexing tradeoffs', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You are indexing legal books for RAG. If you chunk the text into very small blocks (e.g. 10 words), the retrieval captures specific names but loses general argument context. If you chunk into large blocks (e.g. 5000 words), the context is preserved but retrieves too much irrelevant text.', 'question': 'What parameter are you optimizing?', 'correct_answer': 'The text chunk size and overlap configuration.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Optimizing chunk size and chunk overlap ensures the RAG retriever pulls text segments containing both specific details and context.', 'incorrect': 'Temperature handles randomness. SQL tables and content filters do not manage vector search text chunk sizes.', 'concept': 'Chunking strategies in RAG architectures.'}, 'avg_time': 65, 'confused_services': ['chunking', 'temperature'], 'options': ['The text chunk size and overlap configuration.', 'The API temperature parameter.', 'The database SQL table layout.', 'The content filtering safety thresholds.']},
        {'id': 'Q153', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Python SDK: Azure AI Document Intelligence Credentials', 'type': 'dropdown-hotspot', 'scenario': 'A developer is initializing the Python SDK client to connect to a deployed Azure AI Document Intelligence resource. Complete the Python snippet to properly initialize the client with the correct credential class.', 'question': 'Select the correct packages and credentials from the dropdowns.', 'correct_answer': ['azure.core.credentials', 'AzureKeyCredential(key)'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'In the Azure SDK framework, AzureKeyCredential is imported from azure.core.credentials, and is used to wrap API keys to authenticate clients.', 'incorrect': 'azure.identity contains Active Directory tokens (like DefaultAzureCredential). TokenCredential and AzureIdentityCredential are not valid key credentials.', 'concept': 'Document Intelligence SDK authentication.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['python-sdk', 'doc-intel'], 'parts': [{'text': 'from azure.ai.formrecognizer import DocumentAnalysisClient\nfrom ', 'options': ['azure.core.credentials', 'azure.identity', 'azure.ai.formrecognizer'], 'answer': 'azure.core.credentials'}, {'text': ' import AzureKeyCredential\n\nendpoint = "https://myres.cognitiveservices.azure.com/"\nkey = "my-secret-key"\n\nclient = DocumentAnalysisClient(\n    endpoint=endpoint,\n    credential=', 'options': ['AzureKeyCredential(key)', 'TokenCredential(key)', 'AzureIdentityCredential(key)'], 'answer': 'AzureKeyCredential(key)'}]},
        {'id': 'Q154', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Python SDK: Azure Speech audio inputs', 'type': 'dropdown-hotspot', 'scenario': 'A developer is writing code to recognize audio from a local WAV file instead of using the default microphone. Complete the parameters inside AudioConfig and SpeechRecognizer.', 'question': 'Select the correct parameters from the dropdown options.', 'correct_answer': ['filename', 'audio_config'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'AudioConfig(filename="...") is used to load a wav audio file, and it is passed to SpeechRecognizer using the keyword argument audio_config.', 'incorrect': 'device_name is for microphone indices. input_config and stream do not map to the speech recognizer audio parameters directly.', 'concept': 'Azure Speech SDK audio input configurations.'}, 'avg_time': 60, 'confused_services': ['python-sdk', 'speech-config'], 'parts': [{'text': 'from azure.cognitiveservices.speech import SpeechConfig, SpeechRecognizer, AudioConfig\n\nspeech_config = SpeechConfig(subscription="key", region="eastus")\naudio_config = AudioConfig(', 'options': ['filename', 'device_name', 'stream'], 'answer': 'filename'}, {'text': '="recording.wav")\n\nrecognizer = SpeechRecognizer(\n    speech_config=speech_config,\n    ', 'options': ['audio_config', 'input_config', 'stream'], 'answer': 'audio_config'}]},
        {'id': 'Q155', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Python SDK: Azure OpenAI Embeddings', 'type': 'dropdown-hotspot', 'scenario': 'A developer is converting user search terms into vector coordinates using a text embedding model on Azure OpenAI. Complete the Python SDK call to generate embeddings.', 'question': 'Select the correct methods and parameters from the dropdowns.', 'correct_answer': ['embeddings', 'input'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'In the OpenAI v1+ Python SDK, embeddings are generated via client.embeddings.create where the text is passed to the parameter named input.', 'incorrect': 'completions is for text chat results. prompt and query are parameters for completion calls, not embedding requests.', 'concept': 'Azure OpenAI Embeddings SDK syntax.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['python-sdk', 'embeddings'], 'parts': [{'text': 'from openai import AzureOpenAI\nclient = AzureOpenAI(api_key="key", api_version="2024-02-15-preview", azure_endpoint="https://myres.openai.azure.com/")\n\nresponse = client.', 'options': ['embeddings', 'models', 'completions'], 'answer': 'embeddings'}, {'text': '.create(\n    model="my-embeddings-deployment",\n    ', 'options': ['input', 'prompt', 'query'], 'answer': 'input'}]},
        {'id': 'Q156', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Python SDK: Azure AI Language Sentiment results', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A developer is using the Azure AI Language SDK to analyze customer feedback:\n`from azure.ai.textanalytics import TextAnalyticsClient`\n`from azure.core.credentials import AzureKeyCredential`\n`client = TextAnalyticsClient(endpoint=endpoint, credential=AzureKeyCredential(key))`\n`response = client.analyze_sentiment(documents=["The service was fast and friendly!"])`\n`doc = response[0]`\nHow should the developer access the confidence scores of the sentiment?', 'question': 'Select the correct property.', 'correct_answer': 'doc.confidence_scores', 'explanations': {'correct': 'The sentiment analysis document result object contains a property named confidence_scores containing the positive, neutral, and negative decimals.', 'incorrect': 'sentiment_scores, get_scores(), and sentiment.confidence are not properties supported by the Azure AI Language SDK result schema.', 'concept': 'Accessing sentiment confidence scores in SDK.'}, 'avg_time': 40, 'confused_services': ['python-sdk', 'language-client'], 'options': ['doc.confidence_scores', 'doc.sentiment_scores', 'doc.get_scores()', 'doc.sentiment.confidence']},
        {'id': 'Q157', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Responsible AI: Transparency & Accountability', 'type': 'multi-choice', 'scenario': 'A shipping company plans to implement an AI system to predict vehicle maintenance requirements. They need to ensure that the system provides clear insights into which features (such as engine hours, oil age, or climate) had the greatest impact on a prediction, while also appointing an engineering board to review wrong choices.', 'question': 'Which two Responsible AI principles are directly addressed by this implementation strategy? (Select TWO)', 'options': ['Transparency', 'Inclusiveness', 'Accountability', 'Fairness', 'Reliability and Safety'], 'correct_answer': ['Transparency', 'Accountability'], 'explanations': {'correct': 'Providing clear feature insights maps to Transparency. Appointing an engineering review board to take ownership of mistakes maps to Accountability.', 'incorrect': 'Fairness deals with demographic equality, inclusiveness with disability accessibility, and safety with preventing mechanical or operational harm.', 'concept': 'Responsible AI principles.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['transparency', 'accountability']},
        {'id': 'Q158', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Responsible AI: Fairness', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A healthcare organization trains an automated diagnostic tool using patient data gathered from a single region. When deployed globally, the tool produces a high error rate for patients from differing demographic backgrounds.', 'question': 'Which Responsible AI principle was primarily omitted during model training?', 'options': ['Privacy and Security', 'Fairness', 'Transparency', 'Accountability'], 'correct_answer': 'Fairness', 'explanations': {'correct': "Fairness requires that AI models perform equitably across different groups. Training on a single region's demographics causes performance disparities, violating fairness.", 'incorrect': 'Privacy, transparency, and accountability do not directly target demographic parity.', 'concept': 'Demographic bias and fairness.'}, 'avg_time': 35, 'confused_services': ['fairness', 'transparency']},
        {'id': 'Q159', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Responsible AI: Inclusiveness', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'An e-commerce portal launches a digital shopper assistant.', 'question': 'To align with the principle of Inclusiveness, what feature must the development team integrate?', 'options': ['Enforce multi-factor authentication for all customer profiles.', 'Provide a text-to-speech option and high-contrast screen reader compatibility layout structures.', 'Publish the exact statistical weights used by the recommendation engine.', 'Limit automated chat history storage to exactly 30 days.'], 'correct_answer': 'Provide a text-to-speech option and high-contrast screen reader compatibility layout structures.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Inclusiveness requires designing AI applications so that they are accessible to users of all abilities, including those with visual or auditory impairments.', 'incorrect': 'Authentication maps to security, publishing weights maps to transparency, and storage limits relate to privacy.', 'concept': 'Inclusiveness accessibility guidelines.'}, 'avg_time': 35, 'confused_services': ['inclusiveness', 'transparency']},
        {'id': 'Q160', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Python SDK: Content Safety Authentication', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You are implementing an AI core integration script in Python. Review the following code segment:\nfrom azure.core.credentials import AzureKeyCredential\nfrom azure.ai.contentsafety import ContentSafetyClient\nendpoint_uri = "https://safety-demo.cognitiveservices.azure.com/"\napi_key = "SAMPLE_KEY_STRING"\n# Instantiation step\nclient = ContentSafetyClient(endpoint=endpoint_uri, credential=____________________)', 'question': 'Which object wrapper must be typed in the blank spaces to achieve successful authentication using the raw key string?', 'options': ['AzureKeyCredential(api_key)', 'ServiceTokenAuth(api_key)', 'DefaultAzureCredential()', 'ClientSecretCredential(api_key)'], 'correct_answer': 'AzureKeyCredential(api_key)', 'explanations': {'correct': 'In Azure AI SDKs, keys are wrapped in an instance of the AzureKeyCredential class imported from azure.core.credentials.', 'incorrect': 'DefaultAzureCredential is for Active Directory tokens. ClientSecretCredential is for service principals. ServiceTokenAuth does not exist.', 'concept': 'Azure AI key credential classes.'}, 'avg_time': 40, 'confused_services': ['python-sdk', 'content-safety']},
        {'id': 'Q161', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Responsible AI: Reliability and Safety', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': "An autonomous warehousing vehicle uses an onboard AI model to avoid collisions. When a factory power grid flickers, the vehicle's telemetry stream drops out, causing the vehicle to spin in circles instead of executing a safe structural shutdown.", 'question': 'This failure represents a violation of which framework principle?', 'options': ['Fairness', 'Transparency', 'Reliability and Safety', 'Inclusiveness'], 'correct_answer': 'Reliability and Safety', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Reliability and Safety dictates that AI systems should be robust, operate reliably in unexpected conditions, and fail-safe during hardware dropouts.', 'incorrect': 'Fairness, transparency, and inclusiveness are not concerned with safe failover procedures.', 'concept': 'Failover safety in AI systems.'}, 'avg_time': 40, 'confused_services': ['reliability', 'fairness']},
        {'id': 'Q162', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Responsible AI: Privacy & Security', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A corporate legal application reviews employee communications to find contract leaks. An internal audit reveals that the application is scanning non-work personal emails without employee consent, making this data accessible to the IT department.', 'question': 'Which principle is violated?', 'options': ['Privacy and Security', 'Inclusiveness', 'Transparency', 'Accountability'], 'correct_answer': 'Privacy and Security', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Scanning personal emails without explicit consent and exposing private files represents a direct violation of user privacy and data security boundaries.', 'incorrect': 'Inclusiveness, transparency, and accountability do not deal with personal data surveillance.', 'concept': 'Data privacy constraints.'}, 'avg_time': 35, 'confused_services': ['privacy-security', 'accountability']},
        {'id': 'Q163', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Responsible AI: Transparency', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A banking group drafts an artificial intelligence code of conduct stating that all credit denial algorithms must output a human-readable list explaining why an application was rejected.', 'question': 'This resolution satisfies which specific pillar?', 'options': ['Reliability and Safety', 'Inclusiveness', 'Transparency', 'Accountability'], 'correct_answer': 'Transparency', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Providing understandable explanations for automated choices is a primary requirement of system explainability, which maps directly to Transparency.', 'incorrect': 'Reliability, inclusiveness, and accountability do not target explainability directly.', 'concept': 'System explainability.'}, 'avg_time': 30, 'confused_services': ['transparency', 'accountability']},
        {'id': 'Q164', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Python SDK: HTTP Exceptions', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You execute an Azure AI client-side execution block in Python but receive an HTTP Status 403 (Forbidden) exception response code.', 'question': 'Which condition represents the most probable architectural mistake?', 'options': ['The text payload characters exceeded the maximum capacity limit.', 'The endpoint URL string points to an invalid cloud region domain.', 'The underlying Azure AI service resource has been disabled, or the client IP is blocked by the service firewall.', 'The local python runtime environment version is incompatible.'], 'correct_answer': 'The underlying Azure AI service resource has been disabled, or the client IP is blocked by the service firewall.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'HTTP 403 (Forbidden) occurs when authorization fails, which typically means the API key is incorrect, the resource is disabled, or network security rules/firewalls are blocking the IP.', 'incorrect': 'Payload size limits throw HTTP 413. Invalid domain names throw network lookup errors. Python version issues cause compilation errors.', 'concept': 'Azure client HTTP status codes.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['firewall', 'endpoint']},
        {'id': 'Q165', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Machine Learning: Unsupervised Learning', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'Which term describes an operational machine learning layout where an algorithm models properties from a data collection that contains input features but does not provide pre-assigned historical target label answers?', 'question': 'Select the correct learning type.', 'options': ['Supervised Regression', 'Binary Classification', 'Unsupervised Clustering', 'Single-Agent Orchestration'], 'correct_answer': 'Unsupervised Clustering', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Unsupervised learning trains models on datasets without target labels to discover internal structures, such as clustering.', 'incorrect': 'Regression and classification are supervised (rely on labeled data). Single-agent orchestration is a generative AI design.', 'concept': 'Supervised vs unsupervised learning.'}, 'avg_time': 30, 'confused_services': ['clustering', 'regression']},
        {'id': 'Q166', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Machine Learning: Regression', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': "A telemetry dashboard must analyze an office building's historical daily electrical grid demand load to predict tomorrow's energy consumption metrics in total kilowatt-hours.", 'question': 'What type of machine learning task is required?', 'options': ['Multi-class Classification', 'Clustering', 'Regression', 'Binary Classification'], 'correct_answer': 'Regression', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Kilowatt-hours is a continuous numeric value. Predicting numbers maps to Regression.', 'incorrect': 'Classification outputs discrete labels (e.g. true/false or departments). Clustering is unlabeled grouping.', 'concept': 'Regression continuous outputs.'}, 'avg_time': 35, 'confused_services': ['regression', 'classification']},
        {'id': 'Q167', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure AI Foundry: AutoML Pipeline', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You plan to use the automated machine learning (AutoML) interface within Microsoft AI Foundry to construct a model. Which sequence represents the correct order of operations to complete an AutoML pipeline run?\nActions:\nX: Assign the specific target column label intended for prediction.\nY: Deploy the highest performing trained model to a live managed real-time endpoint.\nZ: Register or upload the required data source into the project workspace assets storage.\nW: Choose the primary machine learning task type (e.g., Regression or Classification).', 'question': 'Select the correct sequence order option.', 'options': ['Z → W → X → Y', 'W → Z → X → Y', 'Z → X → W → Y', 'X → W → Z → Y'], 'correct_answer': 'Z → W → X → Y', 'explanations': {'correct': 'First, upload the dataset (Z). Choose the ML task type (W). Assign target columns (X). Finally, deploy the best model endpoint (Y).', 'incorrect': 'You must load dataset Z before setting target columns X or running tasks.', 'concept': 'AutoML lifecycle.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['automl', 'deployment']},
        {'id': 'Q168', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Automated ML: Metric Selection', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You review the evaluation metrics of four predictive model experiments trained via Automated ML. You want to deploy the candidate model that shows the lowest average absolute deviation from the true validation data points.', 'question': 'Which metric target should you prioritize minimizing?', 'options': ['R-Squared (R²)', 'Accuracy', 'Mean Absolute Error (MAE)', 'F1-Score'], 'correct_answer': 'Mean Absolute Error (MAE)', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Mean Absolute Error measures the average magnitude of prediction errors without considering their direction, indicating absolute deviation.', 'incorrect': 'R2 measures variance alignment (maximized). Accuracy and F1-score are classification metrics (maximized).', 'concept': 'Regression metrics evaluation.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['mae', 'r-squared']},
        {'id': 'Q169', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Machine Learning: Clustering', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A streaming media provider wants to look at user viewing profiles to group subscribers into five distinct lifestyle segments (e.g., Sports Enthusiasts, Film Noir Fans) without using any pre-assigned group labels.', 'question': 'Which machine learning task should they implement?', 'options': ['Linear Regression', 'Clustering', 'Multiclass Classification', 'Time-series Forecasting'], 'correct_answer': 'Clustering', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Grouping unlabeled items based on mutual features is clustering (an unsupervised workload).', 'incorrect': 'Linear regression predicts values. Multiclass classification requires pre-labeled training classes.', 'concept': 'Clustering.'}, 'avg_time': 35, 'confused_services': ['clustering', 'classification']},
        {'id': 'Q170', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Classification Metrics: Accuracy Trap', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You train a classification model on an extremely imbalanced dataset where 98% of credit card transactions are genuine and only 2% are fraudulent. The model simply classifies every transaction as "Genuine," resulting in an overall metric score of 0.98.', 'question': 'Which metric provides a misleading impression of performance in this case?', 'options': ['Precision', 'Recall', 'Accuracy', 'F1-Score'], 'correct_answer': 'Accuracy', 'explanations': {'correct': 'On heavily imbalanced datasets, Accuracy is misleading because predicting the majority class always results in high accuracy despite missing the target minor class.', 'incorrect': 'Precision, Recall, and F1-score evaluate prediction quality of positive targets (fraud) and would correctly reveal a score of 0.', 'concept': 'Imbalanced datasets metrics.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['accuracy', 'f1-score']},
        {'id': 'Q171', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'hard', 'topic': 'Classification Metrics: Recall', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A hospital deploys an AI model to detect micro-fractures in bone scans. If the model misses a fracture (a False Negative), the patient goes untreated, risking severe injury. The medical team wants to ensure that out of all true fractures present, the system misses as close to zero as possible.', 'question': 'Which metric must be maximized?', 'options': ['Precision', 'Recall', 'R-Squared (R²)', 'Mean Absolute Error (MAE)'], 'correct_answer': 'Recall', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Recall measures the proportion of actual positive cases (true fractures) correctly identified, minimizing False Negatives.', 'incorrect': 'Precision minimizes false positives. R2 and MAE are regression metrics.', 'concept': 'Optimizing Recall for safety.'}, 'avg_time': 50, 'confused_services': ['recall', 'precision']},
        {'id': 'Q172', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Machine Learning: Multiclass Classification', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A classification model scans incoming support tickets and sorts each ticket into exactly one of three target departments: "Hardware," "Billing," or "Network Support."', 'question': 'What type of machine learning task does this represent?', 'options': ['Binary Classification', 'Multiclass Classification', 'Unsupervised Clustering', 'Linear Regression'], 'correct_answer': 'Multiclass Classification', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Sorting inputs into one of three or more distinct labeled classes is multiclass classification.', 'incorrect': 'Binary classification has exactly two target classes. Clustering is unsupervised. Regression outputs numbers.', 'concept': 'Multiclass classification.'}, 'avg_time': 30, 'confused_services': ['multiclass', 'binary']},
        {'id': 'Q173', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Python SDK: Live Endpoints', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'Review the following Python snippet used to send feature rows to an endpoint deployed via Microsoft AI Foundry:\nimport urllib.request\nimport json\nendpoint_url = "https://demo-endpoint.ml.azure.com/score"\nbearer_token = "SECURE_TOKEN_STRING"\ndata_payload = {"Inputs": {"data": [{"Age": 45, "Income": 62000}]}}\nbody = str.encode(json.dumps(data_payload))\nreq = urllib.request.Request(endpoint_url, body)\nreq.add_header(\'Content-Type\', \'application/json\')\nreq.add_header(\'Authorization\', \'Bearer \' + bearer_token)', 'question': 'What is the primary function of the header string containing the bearer_token variable?', 'options': ['Content features config', "It securely authenticates the client application against the model's live endpoint.", 'Model prediction temperature', 'Downsampling payload scale'], 'correct_answer': "It securely authenticates the client application against the model's live endpoint.", 'explanations': {'correct': 'The Authorization header containing a Bearer token verifies the identity of the client request to access the deployed endpoint.', 'incorrect': 'It does not configure input data, model parameters like temperature, or modify the payload scale.', 'concept': 'Bearer token auth headers.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['authorization', 'payload']},
        {'id': 'Q174', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'easy', 'topic': 'Machine Learning: Features', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'In machine learning terminology, what term describes the structural input data variables or observation attributes passed into a model during training to help it learn predictive behaviors?', 'question': 'Select the correct term.', 'options': ['Labels', 'Features', 'Residuals', 'Endpoints'], 'correct_answer': 'Features', 'explanations': {'correct': 'Features are the independent input variables (e.g. age, square footage) used to make predictions.', 'incorrect': 'Labels are the correct target answers. Residuals are errors. Endpoints are API routes.', 'concept': 'ML inputs.'}, 'avg_time': 30, 'confused_services': ['features', 'labels']},
        {'id': 'Q175', 'objective': 'Objective 1', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Regression Metrics: R-Squared', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'You are evaluating a regression model trained to predict house prices. The dashboard indicates an R-Squared (R²) evaluation value of 0.92.', 'question': 'How should you interpret this result?', 'options': ['The model predicted only 12% of house prices correctly.', 'The model captures 92% of the variance observed within the target evaluation data asset.', 'The average prediction error is exactly $92,000.', 'The model failed to process 8% of the data columns.'], 'correct_answer': 'The model captures 92% of the variance observed within the target evaluation data asset.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'R-Squared measures the proportion of variance in the dependent variable that is predictable from the independent features; a score of 0.92 indicates 92% of the variance is captured.', 'incorrect': 'It is not a direct accuracy percentage, dollar deviation value, or column processing success rate.', 'concept': 'R-Squared correlation measurements.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['r-squared', 'mae']},
