        {'id': 'Q182', 'objective': 'Objective 2', 'difficulty': 'medium', 'topic': 'Azure AI Vision: Spatial Analysis Compliance', 'type': 'single-choice', 'scenario': 'A retail store chain uses Spatial Analysis to track consumer foot-traffic density across different promotional displays.', 'options': ['It stores full-resolution facial photos in public storage buckets.', "It matches shoppers' faces against corporate employee ID databases.", 'It tracks human movement as anonymous geometric shapes without performing facial recognition.', 'It requires visitors to opt-in via a mobile application before entering the camera field of view.'], 'correct_answer': 'It tracks human movement as anonymous geometric shapes without performing facial recognition.', 'explanations': {'correct': 'To ensure privacy compliance, Spatial Analysis tracks human shapes geometrically as polygons/lines and does not capture or store unique facial identity records.', 'incorrect': 'Storing photos or matching face shapes violates privacy principles.', 'concept': 'Spatial analysis privacy defaults.'}, 'avg_time': 45, 'confused_services': ['spatial-analysis', 'face'], 'question': 'To comply with privacy guidelines, how does the Spatial Analysis service process data frames from camera feeds by default?'},
